WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.953
- Do you wanna be friends?

00:00:00.953 --> 00:00:01.786
Friends?

00:00:01.786 --> 00:00:02.619
Friends?

00:00:02.619 --> 00:00:04.710
I'm a liberal and I tried
to make 100 new friends

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.360
at a Trump rally in Tennessee.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.680
But what I thought was just gonna be

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:09.060
like this goofy adventure-

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:10.920
- We were abducted by aliens.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:11.753
- Really?

00:00:11.753 --> 00:00:13.710
turned into something much darker

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:16.088
and it completely changed
how I view America.

00:00:16.088 --> 00:00:18.838
(crowd chanting)

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:21.120
But let me back up.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.110
I live in Los Angeles,

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:23.777
which is one of the most
liberal cities in the country.

00:00:23.777 --> 00:00:26.557
I feel like in LA, some people are like,

00:00:26.557 --> 00:00:27.930
"If you're a Trump supporter,

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:28.840
I don't wanna be friends with you."

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:30.750
Would you fall into that camp?

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:31.830
- Yes!

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:32.760
- [Sam] And when I try to make

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.440
100 new friends at UCLA,

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:35.280
it went pretty well.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.323
I even made some lasting friendships,

00:00:38.653 --> 00:00:39.630
(cheers)

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:41.460
but maybe it's easier 'cause I'm in LA.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:42.990
What about America at large?

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:45.150
Where it feels like we're
more polarized than ever.

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:47.460
So, I wanted to try this experiment again

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:50.700
and see if liberals and Trump
supporters could be friends,

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.500
which is why I flew to Memphis, Tennessee

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.690
and bought a ticket to
attend a Trump rally,

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:57.180
AKA the American Freedom Tour.

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:59.220
And holy (bleep), these
tickets are expensive.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:00.540
Oh. and Malik is coming with me,

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:02.190
but he seemed a bit nervous.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:04.394
How are you feeling about
going to a Trump rally?

00:01:04.394 --> 00:01:07.440
(crowd yelling)

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:09.556
- I'm not prepared for any of that.

00:01:09.556 --> 00:01:12.193
(crowd yelling)

00:01:12.193 --> 00:01:13.710
- [Sam] I didn't feel prepared either.

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:15.600
So to give our adventure some purpose,

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.580
I created a quest list.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:18.930
I wanted to meet a celebrity,

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:20.580
have a meal with a Trump supporter,

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.860
get a Trump supporter to
invite me into their home.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:24.630
And since I'm entering Bible Belt,

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:26.520
I figured let's try to go
to church with someone.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:27.900
With our quest mapped out,

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:30.360
I got ready to meet Malik
for a 6:00 AM flight.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:32.171
We meet again. (laughs)

00:01:32.171 --> 00:01:33.004
Where are you guys from?

00:01:33.004 --> 00:01:33.837
- I'm from Thailand.

00:01:33.837 --> 00:01:34.803
- I love Thailand!

00:01:36.802 --> 00:01:38.282
We have landed in Memphis.

00:01:38.282 --> 00:01:39.115
- [Woman] Mr Norman?

00:01:39.115 --> 00:01:39.948
- Yep, that's me.
- [Woman] Hi how are you?

00:01:39.948 --> 00:01:43.828
- 1000% going to have to do
a montage with this truck.

00:01:43.828 --> 00:01:45.102
♪ Oh, the fast life ♪

00:01:45.102 --> 00:01:46.374
♪ The fast living ♪
♪ Fast living ♪

00:01:46.374 --> 00:01:47.300
♪ They see the ambition ♪

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.966
♪ They know I'm past driven ♪
♪ Skrrt! ♪

00:01:48.966 --> 00:01:49.966
♪ Look we are not the same ♪

00:01:49.966 --> 00:01:51.422
♪ This is not a game ♪
♪ Not a game ♪

00:01:51.422 --> 00:01:52.255
♪ I be swerving ♪

00:01:52.255 --> 00:01:53.160
- Truck.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:55.140
As I adjusted to this massive truck

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:57.090
and the ridiculously
warm weather of Memphis,

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:58.530
I was getting more and more stressed.

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:00.510
The more I thought about what I had to do.

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:03.630
So to calm my nerves, I
called my ex-girlfriend.

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:04.463
- Hello.

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:06.143
- Hey.

00:02:06.143 --> 00:02:08.610
- Like, I don't have any
clue what I'm doing here.

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:11.160
- You should probably walk
around Memphis today to get a

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:12.360
feeling for the city.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:13.740
It's like, you haven't talked to anybody.

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:15.000
You don't actually know
what the people are like.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.650
You've never been to this place.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.810
Get like culturally aware?

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:20.040
- [Sam] Honestly, great advice.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:21.814
Quick question.
- [Woman] Yeah.

00:02:21.814 --> 00:02:24.360
- Do you think LA or
Memphis is friendlier?

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:25.620
- Oh, Memphis for sure.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:26.580
- [Sam] Why?

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:28.500
- Oh, it's just friendlier
people than Los Angeles.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:29.850
- [Sam] Do you wanna be friends?

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:30.683
- No.

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:31.590
- I've been to Gold.
- I feel like the people in LA

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:33.660
are assholes, so probably Memphis.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:34.493
- I'm from LA.

00:02:34.493 --> 00:02:36.870
- LA, cause you can smoke more kush there.

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:38.550
- Yo, you're drunk. Quit.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:39.383
Memphis sucks.

00:02:39.383 --> 00:02:40.560
I've lived here all my life.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.690
- Y'all should come to The Bluff tonight.

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:43.523
- [Sam] What's, what's
happening at The Bluff?

00:02:43.523 --> 00:02:45.390
- You've never been to The
Bluff on a Thursday night?

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:46.645
- This is my first time in Memphis,

00:02:46.645 --> 00:02:47.608
of course I've never been.

00:02:47.608 --> 00:02:48.441
- I'm sorry, I'm-

00:02:48.441 --> 00:02:49.290
- Ask me another question.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:51.030
- I was feeling a pretty friendly energy.

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:54.390
So I told people what the
heck I was doing in Memphis.

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:56.103
I, we have this show
called 100 New Friends.

00:02:56.103 --> 00:02:58.350
- Okay.
- We were at UCLA.

00:02:58.350 --> 00:02:59.790
We like brought 100 people together.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:00.623
- Do you want to be friends?

00:03:00.623 --> 00:03:01.456
- Friends! Friendship.

00:03:01.456 --> 00:03:02.525
(cheering)

00:03:02.525 --> 00:03:04.230
So, now we're trying to do the same thing,

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:05.790
but, like I'm kind of liberal

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:07.260
and I'm doing it at a Trump rally.

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:09.660
- Then, you are not in
the right city my friend.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:10.493
- I love Trump.

00:03:10.493 --> 00:03:11.940
He's just the first president we've had

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.800
that's actually spoke his mind in a while.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:15.720
- Do you think like, it
would be hard for you

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:16.851
to be friends with a liberal?

00:03:16.851 --> 00:03:18.510
- Absolutely not, no.

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:20.550
I feel like a lot of people are too

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:22.290
close-minded on that topic.

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:24.270
They'll kill an entire relationship

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.010
over a political interest.

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:29.070
- Liberals are more like 100%

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:31.762
like, more against Trump supporters.

00:03:31.762 --> 00:03:34.410
(crowd shouting)

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:35.640
- Are you Trump or Biden?

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:36.473
- I'm a liberal.

00:03:36.473 --> 00:03:37.306
- We can be friends though.

00:03:37.306 --> 00:03:38.139
It's just an opinion.
- It's a matter of being-

00:03:38.139 --> 00:03:40.980
- You know Trump's coming
to Memphis tomorrow?

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:41.813
- I'm going.

00:03:41.813 --> 00:03:42.646
- Oh okay, oh!

00:03:42.646 --> 00:03:43.479
Then you'll see me there.

00:03:43.479 --> 00:03:44.312
- Probably won't come.

00:03:44.312 --> 00:03:45.145
- You wanna come?

00:03:45.145 --> 00:03:45.978
- Yeah, I mean. Yeah.

00:03:45.978 --> 00:03:47.190
- Are you supporting Trump or Biden?

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:48.090
- Oh, Trump.

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:48.923
- You going to go to the rally?

00:03:48.923 --> 00:03:50.790
- No.
- Hell yes.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:51.720
- I'm gonna be there.

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:52.638
- Oh God.

00:03:52.638 --> 00:03:54.707
I mean, is this what
the interview is about?

00:03:54.707 --> 00:03:57.390
- I feel like Trump's a
genuinely good human being.

00:03:57.390 --> 00:03:58.223
- Do you think he's sexist?

00:03:58.223 --> 00:03:59.520
- [Trump] Grab 'em by the (bleep).

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:00.387
- Trump? Yeah.

00:04:00.387 --> 00:04:01.830
- And that's what we've needed.

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:03.510
We needed somebody who's
gonna speak their mind.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:05.550
- You need to go to some other people.

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:07.650
- But there was a silver
lining to our night out.

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:08.820
You wanna be friends?

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:10.050
- No.
- No?

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:11.940
- We got too many friends.

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:13.163
- [Announcer] Giving the match!

00:04:13.163 --> 00:04:15.278
Boom! And Lawler with a right hand!

00:04:15.278 --> 00:04:19.110
- [Announcer] Jerry, The King, Lawler!

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:20.520
- [Sam] It was pretty
cool that we met famed

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:22.800
WWE announcer, Jerry Lawler.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:24.360
But I still couldn't shake the feeling

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:25.470
that I was out of my depth.

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:28.050
- Do you think LA or
Memphis is more friendly?

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:30.300
- Probably LA because people get shot

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:31.500
in Memphis all the time.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:34.590
- We were down here last weekend
and three people got shot.

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:35.423
- Why?

00:04:35.423 --> 00:04:36.570
- Crime rate's high.

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:37.403
It's Memphis.

00:04:37.403 --> 00:04:40.590
- This place is the most
unsafe city in the nation.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:41.700
- Just be careful-
I'm about to get a taxi.

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:43.410
- Do you have a bulletproof vest?

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:44.670
- I don't, I don't.

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:47.820
I feel like the resounding
advice from this trip has been,

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:48.653
- Don't go to Memphis.

00:04:48.653 --> 00:04:50.910
- Why would you say Memphis is not good?

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:51.960
- Crime.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:54.090
Memphis nowadays, it's number one.

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:57.030
- New study finds Memphis
is the most dangerous

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:57.990
city in the country.

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:00.210
This report comes as the Bluff City

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:03.518
is on pace to surpass a
record number of homicides.

00:05:03.518 --> 00:05:06.420
(suspenseful music)

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:07.470
- [Sam] In an effort to get some thoughts

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:08.370
from the other side of the aisle,

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:10.020
I decided to follow some sage wisdom

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:10.890
I got the night before.

00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:12.023
- Go to Rhodes Campus.

00:05:12.023 --> 00:05:14.850
They're not Trump
anywhere near that school.

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:16.710
- I'd never heard of Rhodes before,

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:19.563
but they said it really puts
the liberal in liberal arts.

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:23.853
Campus is beautiful, but
there is no one here.

00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:26.183
Hey, excuse me.

00:05:26.183 --> 00:05:27.210
Do you guys wanna be friends?

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:28.043
- I'm cool with you.

00:05:28.043 --> 00:05:28.876
- Sure, What's your name?

00:05:28.876 --> 00:05:29.856
- Ricky.
- Isaac.

00:05:29.856 --> 00:05:31.290
- Isaac.
- Robin.

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:32.280
- Robin.
- Julia.

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:33.600
- Julia.
- Harrison.

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:34.433
- Harrison.

00:05:34.433 --> 00:05:35.567
How did you guys all meet each other?

00:05:35.567 --> 00:05:36.996
- Orientation.
- Do you go here?

00:05:36.996 --> 00:05:38.520
- No, I go to UCLA actually.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:40.410
Turns out Ricky was an incoming freshman.

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:41.243
Super nice guy.

00:05:41.243 --> 00:05:43.830
Philosophy major, liked
to ponder about the world.

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:46.860
And I had just stumbled upon orientation.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:49.260
- [Man] Ready to meet the
challenge of college life.

00:05:49.260 --> 00:05:51.480
- I've met a lot of people
from, like, both extremes

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:52.590
and, uh,
- Yeah.

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:53.820
- at the end of the day, I mean,

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:55.140
that's not really what it comes down to.

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:56.760
It comes down to, like,
who they actually are.

00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:57.960
I just don't get into politics.

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:59.220
- It's not exactly someone's house,

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:00.630
but we kinda got invited to dinner.

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:03.870
I would call it, having
a meal with a Memphisian.

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:04.740
Mission accomplished.

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:07.170
We might not be able
to get like 100 people.

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:08.370
We're learning a lot about Memphis.

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:09.203
Excuse me.

00:06:09.203 --> 00:06:10.036
Do you guys wanna be friends?

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:11.280
- [Woman] Yes!

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:12.113
- Sick!

00:06:12.113 --> 00:06:13.350
- My name's Sam.

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:14.820
Beatrix, nice to meet you.

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:15.670
Sage, nice to meet to you.

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:18.057
This is Malik. Are you guys friends?

00:06:18.057 --> 00:06:19.412
- No.
- Yeah?

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:21.186
- Oh.
(laughs)

00:06:21.186 --> 00:06:22.019
- [Sam] Beatrix!

00:06:22.019 --> 00:06:23.850
- We'll be friends after Sage graduates.

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:24.683
- Yeah.
- [Sam] Okay.

00:06:24.683 --> 00:06:26.250
- [Narrator] A few moments later.

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:27.570
I don't really talk to Trump supporters.

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:29.820
And so I'm, there's a
rally here on Saturday.

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:31.050
- A word of advice.

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:31.950
I say tread lightly.

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:34.350
Not because these people
are like, super dangerous

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:35.790
or like, anything like that.

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:37.830
I think the people that
you are going to meet

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:39.870
believe what they believe for a reason.

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:41.040
Before you can have a conversation,

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:43.560
you have to have an element
of respect and understanding.

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:45.090
- Do you think you could be
friends with a Trump supporter?

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:47.910
- Probably have friends that
are Trump supporters right now.

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:50.550
But I also see like holding
the beliefs of hatred is

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:52.800
negative, negatively affecting the person

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:53.730
that holds those beliefs.

00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:56.790
The Southern experience is not a monolith.

00:06:56.790 --> 00:06:58.320
Like, you are probably not going

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:00.735
to find a lot of Trump
supporters in this area at all.

00:07:00.735 --> 00:07:01.568
- Yeah.

00:07:01.568 --> 00:07:04.005
We went down to Beale Street yesterday

00:07:04.005 --> 00:07:05.414
- (chuckles) Yep.
and it was like 50/50.

00:07:05.414 --> 00:07:06.331
- Uh, Trump.

00:07:06.331 --> 00:07:07.164
- I'm liberal.

00:07:07.164 --> 00:07:08.040
- I love Trump.

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:09.060
- Beale Street is probably not

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:10.770
super representative of Memphis.

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:14.130
You might find like,
people don't exactly vibe

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:15.090
with someone from LA

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:17.010
coming out with like fancy tech equipment

00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:18.780
to like, talk about things.
- Yeah.

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:19.613
- I mean like, what are,

00:07:19.613 --> 00:07:21.627
what are you doing on Saturday?

00:07:21.627 --> 00:07:22.460
- I mean,

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:23.293
I'm doing Juneteenth things

00:07:23.293 --> 00:07:25.050
and I'm not gonna invite
a white guy from LA.

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:27.030
Like, think about it for
like two and a half seconds

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:28.080
and it will make so much sense.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:28.913
- [Announcer] Match, boom!

00:07:29.861 --> 00:07:32.278
(calm music)

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:37.890
- Right now we're at the hotel where

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:41.190
Martin Luther king was assassinated.

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:46.190
- We must also realize that the
problems of racial injustice

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:51.090
and economic injustice cannot
be solved without a radical

00:07:51.090 --> 00:07:55.050
redistribution of political
and economic power.

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:55.994
- What was your name?

00:07:55.994 --> 00:07:57.200
- Murray.
- Murray. Sam.

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:59.940
- And they are the very people
telling the black man that he

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:02.850
ought to lift himself
by his own bootstraps.

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:05.040
- As you see with the people around here,

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:07.043
economics is a problem.
- Mm.

00:08:07.043 --> 00:08:09.660
And I mean, people are just people,

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:14.400
which is why I just don't really
think that politics is ever

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:17.100
gonna work the way it's set up.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:20.100
'Cause we just elect these
people to represent us.

